Only cash that reaches holders counts: the buybacks measured on chain above, annualised from the last 13 weeks to {hcf} a year. The model (`settlemark/valuation.py`) grows that cash for {ny1} years, fades growth to {tg} over {ny2} more, and discounts at {dr}. Growth is not typed by hand: the bull case is the observed annualised revenue growth of the last half year ({gobs}) capped at {gbull}; base is half of that ({gbase}); bear is no growth.

